hb.act.n=§4Act %s
hb.act.1.name=§fJoined the Game
hb.act.1.intro=§7Someone joined the game. There is nobody else in this world.
hb.act.1.text=First, the noises: footsteps that aren't there, a door, your name.\n\nThen, in the chat: §eGreen Steve joined the game§r. At night someone knocks on your door, three slow knocks, and waits for you to open it: §fThe Knocker§r. And in the dark corner of the room a husky sits and smiles at you with human teeth: §fSmile Dog§r.\n\nSomeone was in this world before you. What they built is still out there, and in each place they left a note.
hb.act.2.name=§fThe Others
hb.act.2.intro=§7They aren't just stories any more. There are others, and they know where you are.
hb.act.2.text=At the back of the caves, among crosses of stone, something standing in a white mask: §fThe Lick§r.\n\nLines with your name on them appear in the chat, things you never wrote. Something far too tall mimics you from the trees: §fThe Mimicer§r.\n\nA numbers station on a dead frequency, and a red figure five blocks tall out in the field. Don't look at it: §fThe Boiled One§r.\n\nThe lights in your house go out one by one. Someone whispers: "Go to sleep." §fJeff the Killer§r.
hb.act.3.name=§fThe Pages
hb.act.3.intro=§7The fog comes in. There are pages pinned to the trees.
hb.act.3.text=One foggy night eight pages appear, pinned to the trunks around you. Tear them all down.\n\nWith every page the drums get louder, the fog thicker, and he is closer: very tall, very thin, a black suit and no face. §fSlenderman§r.\n\nDon't look at him. Looking brings the static, and the static hurts. If he reaches you, or time runs out, the wind takes the pages.\n\nFind all eight and he will leave you in peace for a few nights.
