hb.lore.ambience=§lSounds§r\n\nFootsteps behind you, a door, a chest opening by itself, the hiss of a creeper that isn't there, breathing, knocks on the wall, your name whispered. They come from somewhere: you will hear which side.
hb.lore.scares=§lScares§r\n\nA face in front of yours for the length of a blink. Breath on your neck. A door slamming in an empty house. The screen tearing into static. A blow that hurts and leaves no mark.
hb.lore.ruins=§lStructures§r\n\nSomeone was in this world before you. As the days go by you will find what they built: a cabin, a kennel, a field of crosses, a blue temple, a radio mast, a camp. In each there is a chest with a page of their diary. The chat tells you roughly where.
hb.lore.greensteve=§lGreen Steve§r\n\n"Green Steve joined the game." He looks exactly like Steve, but green all over, with blank eyes. He writes "I am coming." Every time you look away he is closer. When he reaches you he says "Hello, brother", and the hissing starts all around you.\n\n§eTip:§r don't take your eyes off him... though staring too long calls him too.
hb.lore.knocker=§lThe Knocker§r\n\nA pale dead thing, too tall and too thin, with long fingers and a hanging mouth. It learns where you live. At night it knocks on your door: three slow knocks, and again. It never comes in on its own: it waits for you to open. If you don't, the knocking stops... and it taps on a window. It knows where you sleep.\n\n§eTip:§r don't open the door.
hb.lore.smiledog=§lSmile Dog§r\n\nA husky sitting in the dark of a room, its muzzle pulled back into a human smile full of human teeth. Look at it too long and it gets into your head: the picture, the flash, the words. SPREAD THE WORD. Then it gets up.\n\n§eTip:§r it can be killed once it runs.
hb.lore.lick=§lThe Lick§r\n\nAt the back of a cave, always at the back, a figure in black standing perfectly still, facing you. A white porcelain mask and a long red tongue hanging out of the smile. Around it, the floor is marked with crosses of stone. It does nothing. Until you come close or shine a light on it.\n\n§eTip:§r it can't be hurt. Get out of the cave.
hb.lore.mimicer=§lThe Mimicer§r\n\nShaped like Steve, but wrong: too tall, arms and legs too long, empty holes for eyes. It talks. In the chat, under YOUR name, it says things you never said; from the trees, it makes villager sounds. Look at it too long, or get too close, and it runs at you on those long legs.\n\n§eTip:§r it can't climb. Build up three blocks.
hb.lore.boiled=§lThe Boiled One§r\n\nDoctor Nowhere. First, the station: a flat voice reading numbers on a frequency nobody uses. Then it is standing in the field: a crimson, withered figure five blocks tall, with a misshapen head and two red points for eyes. Those who look too long suffer the Phenomenon: everything goes red, you can't stand straight, and it hurts.\n\n§eTip:§r DON'T LOOK AT IT.
hb.lore.jeff=§lJeff the Killer§r\n\nWhite hoodie, black hair, a chalk-white face: eyes that can't close and a smile cut into the cheeks. He comes into houses at night. The lights go out one by one and someone whispers, very close: "Go to sleep." If you do, when you wake he is beside the bed.\n\n§eTip:§r he can be killed.
hb.lore.slender=§lSlenderman§r\n\nVery tall, very thin, standing among the trees at the edge of what you can see. Black suit, white shirt, no face. When he wants to, long black tendrils come out of his back. One foggy night he pins eight pages to the trees. Find them all before he finds you.\n\n§eTip:§r don't look at him. When he's behind you, run.
