item.hb:note_1.name=§fNote 1: Day 1
hb.note.1.title=1. Day 1
hb.note.1.text=I started this world to build in peace. New seed, nobody else.\n\nThis afternoon the chat said: "Green Steve joined the game". There is nobody else. I wrote "hello?". He answered: "I am coming."\n\nI saw him at the edge of the forest. It was Steve. But green. All of him. And the eyes blank.\n\nEvery time I looked away, he was closer.
item.hb:note_2.name=§fNote 2: Day 2
hb.note.2.title=2. Day 2
hb.note.2.text=At night someone knocks on the door. Three slow knocks. Then again.\n\nI didn't open it. In the morning there were marks of long fingers in the wood. On the outside.\n\nI call it the Knocker. It doesn't come in unless you open. But it knows where I sleep: last night I woke and it was standing beside the bed.\n\nDon't open the door.
item.hb:note_3.name=§fNote 3: The kennel
hb.note.3.title=3. The kennel
hb.note.3.text=I had a dog. A husky. One night it sat in the dark corner of the room and looked at me.\n\nIt was smiling. Not the way a dog smiles: with human teeth. Rows of them.\n\nDon't look at it for long. After I saw it I could only think of one thing.\n\nSPREAD THE WORD.\n\nIf you are reading this, I already have.
item.hb:note_4.name=§fNote 4: The crosses
hb.note.4.title=4. The crosses
hb.note.4.text=In the caves there are crosses of stone on the floor. And at the back, always at the back, someone is standing.\n\nIn black, with a white mask and a long red tongue hanging out of the smile. It doesn't move.\n\nDon't shine your light on it. Don't go close. It can't be hurt.\n\nI put these crosses up here to remember. Don't go back down.
item.hb:note_5.name=§fNote 5: The blue temple
hb.note.5.title=5. The blue temple
hb.note.5.text=I heard my name from the trees. In my voice.\n\nLines of mine I never wrote come up in the chat: "come here", "i'm over here", "help".\n\nIt's tall. Far too tall. Long arms and legs and holes where the eyes should be. I call it the Mimicer.\n\nIt runs faster than you, but it can't climb. Build up three blocks and it stays at the bottom, looking up.
item.hb:note_6.name=§fNote 6: The mast
hb.note.6.title=6. The mast
hb.note.6.text=The radio picks up a station that doesn't exist. A flat voice reads numbers. Between the numbers, something else.\n\nI built this mast to hear it better. Mistake.\n\nNow I see him: red, burnt, five blocks tall, two red points for eyes, standing in the field. They call him the Boiled One. Doctor Nowhere.\n\nDON'T LOOK AT HIM. Look too long and everything goes red, and it hurts.
item.hb:note_7.name=§fNote 7: The camp
hb.note.7.title=7. The camp
hb.note.7.text=I don't sleep in the cabin any more. He comes into houses.\n\nHe puts the lights out one by one and whispers very close: "Go to sleep." White face, eyes that don't close, the smile cut into the cheeks. Jeff, at least, can be hurt.\n\nTonight there is fog, and there are pages pinned to the trees. Eight. They say if you find them all, he leaves you alone.\n\nI'm going to try.
item.hb:note_8.name=§fNote 8: The last page
hb.note.8.title=8. The last page
hb.note.8.text=If you are reading this, you found all eight. I didn't. I got to seven.\n\nNow I'm in the forest, among the trees, with the others. Watching. I don't have a face any more.\n\nHe'll let you rest for a few nights. Then the fog comes back. It always comes back.\n\n— the one who was here before
